    "text": "The Chiesa di Sant'Urbano alla Caffarella is a historic church in Rome that sits on the site of an ancient Roman temple. Its layered history—from a 2nd‑century pagan shrine to a medieval church and later Baroque restoration—illustrates the city’s architectural evolution and the continuity of sacred space.",
    "sourceIds": ["wikipedia"]
